    {
      "id": "0979554d-4961-4771-a89c-fa439dcee09e",
      "name": "Sticky Note 9be6068a",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automation 03: Low-Stock Reorder Alerts\n\n### Introduction\nEvery hour on weekdays from 8am to 6pm, this workflow checks stock levels and emails procurement a draft purchase order when an item falls below its minimum. No AI is used.\n\n### What to key in\n**Inventory** tab, one row per item: sku, item, category, qty_on_hand, reorder_min, reorder_target. Keep qty_on_hand up to date, and leave alert_sent and last_alert blank.\n**Vendors** tab, one row per item: vendor_id, vendor_name, vendor_email, contact_name, sku, unit_price_sgd, pack_size.\n\n### What happens next\n1. Each item is compared with its minimum.\n2. Low items are grouped by vendor, and order sizes are rounded up to full packs.\n3. The draft is saved in **PO Drafts** and emailed to procurement. It does not go to the vendor.\n4. alert_sent is set to yes, so the same item does not alert again.\n5. After restocking, alert_sent is cleared automatically.\n6. A missing vendor or unreadable number goes to **Exceptions** and procurement once.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Gmail account in **Email Procurement PO** and **Email Vendor Missing**.\n2. In **Config**, enter procurement_email.\n3. Test with test_mode on, which sends every email to test_email.\n4. For live use, set test_mode to false and publish.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 680,
        "height": 760
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Hourly Stock Scan": {
      "main": [
        [
